    gameplay: 'Players draw one tile and discard one tile in turn. Discards may be claimed to form Chow, Pung, or Kong according to claim priority and position restrictions. A player wins by self-draw or discard claim when the hand is complete under table scoring requirements.',
    keyRules: [
      'East starts with 14 tiles; other players start with 13.',
      'Each turn is draw one tile, then discard one tile.',
      "Chow claims are limited to the player on the discarder's left; Pung and Kong can be claimed by any player.",
      'Winning hand structure is four melds and one pair, with fan requirements determined by the table rule set.',
